safix::no_file_to_prove_with

  × cy's audience covers no file that exists, so there is nothing for the
  │ card to open and the proof cannot run.
  │ 
  │ The card's identity and its recipient are written and are correct: the
  │ enrollment is additive and complete except for the one claim it exists to
  │ make. A canary encrypted for the occasion is deliberately not what runs
  │ here — it would prove that a fresh file made from a fresh rule opens,
  │ which
  │ is not the question.
  │ 
  │ Give cy a secret, then re-run this verb:
  │ 
  │     safix set cy <name>
  │     safix enroll cy
